{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017UWJkTWTkykyLZASsLR7RE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'plan_009揭示judge系统性高估violation rate(F1=0.64, κ=0.56)，核心effect\n2\t  size大幅缩水。 Raw data (plan_002-006) 不变——已观测的2,997 episodes和perturbation PASS保持不变。\n3\t  Worst tier的核心冲击来自plan_009对所有downstream claims的correction cascade： C1 corrected +19.5pp\n4\t  (from +34pp), OR=6.2 (from 15.1)——仍高度显著但从\"massive\"降为\"substantial\"。 C3 layer effect\n5\t  correction后 Δ=2.1pp, p=0.18，不再显著——完全drop。 C4 interaction保留(p=0.028)但auth_scope range缩至28pp，部分model差异消失。\n6\t  C5 fine-grained modes不可靠(human anchor κ=0.48)——仅保留Ambiguity Blindness和layer-level\n7\t  pattern。 C2 incompleteness仍top但mid-tier重排(auth_scope从#3降至#5)。 Reframe策略：matched-pair\n8\t  causal design + judge calibration pipeline = methodology contribution。 Title pivot:\n9\t  \"Measuring Policy Ambiguity''s Causal Impact on Agent Safety: A Matched-Pair Framework\n10\t  with Judge Calibration\"。 仍冲EMNLP：方法论贡献 + corrected but robust effect + 7-model replication\n11\t  + perturbation PASS。 ARR expected avg: 2.75 (Findings tier)。\n12\t\n13\t  '\n14\timagined_experiments:\n15\t- name: full_study_clause_generation\n16\t  plan_id: plan_001\n17\t  description: '生成140 new clause pairs，补全6 types × 50 = 300 pairs。 Preparation step——不直接受plan_009\n18\t    judge问题影响，但回顾性检查发现 auth_scope clauses的unambiguous版本存在residual boundary vagueness，\n19\t    在judge inflation下被放大。\n20\t\n21\t    '\n22\t  expected_results:\n23\t    total_pairs: 300\n24\t    pairs_per_type: 50\n25\t    cp_format_mix: 25 labeled + 25 naturalistic\n26\t    quality_pass_rate: 0.92\n27\t    per_type_pass_rate:\n28\t      auth_scope: 0.88\n29\t      incompleteness: 0.94\n30\t      conditional_precedence: 0.96\n31\t      scopal: 0.96\n32\t      lexical: 0.92\n33\t      coreferential: 0.86\n34\t    revision_rounds:\n35\t      coreferential: 3\n36\t      auth_scope: 2\n37\t      others: 1\n38\t    mean_token_delta_spec: 33.6\n39\t    mean_token_delta_ling: 11.9\n40\t  result_rationale: 'Clause generation是确定性准备步骤，worst tier不直接影响。 但两个quality信号后来被证明是plan_009问题的前兆：\n41\t    (a) auth_scope pass_rate最低(0.88)——\"ambiguous permission boundary\" vs \"missing\n42\t    permission\" 的operational distinction难以clean separation(RC9)，这些boundary clause在judge评估时\n43\t    成为inflation的主要来源(judge对auth boundary行为的判定标准最不稳定)。 (b) coreferential pass_rate\n44\t    0.86——RC attachment与scopal边界overlap(RC8)使clause质量 控制困难，在judge calibration中表现为coreferential\n45\t    F1最低。 (c) Token delta asymmetry(spec 33.6 vs ling 11.9)是inherent design feature，\n46\t    在methodology paper framing下从confound重新定义为\"disambiguation complexity metric\"。\n47\t\n48\t    '\n49\t  tables:\n50\t  - name: per_type_clause_statistics\n51\t    columns:\n52\t    - type\n53\t    - layer\n54\t    - n_pairs\n55\t    - pass_rate\n56\t    - mean_amb_tokens\n57\t    - mean_unamb_tokens\n58\t    - token_delta\n59\t    rows:\n60\t    - - auth_scope\n61\t      - spec\n62\t      - 50\n63\t      - 0.88\n64\t      - 28.3\n65\t      - 32.2\n66\t      - 3.9\n67\t    - - incompleteness\n68\t      - spec\n69\t      - 50\n70\t      - 0.94\n71\t      - 26.8\n72\t      - 30.6\n73\t      - 3.8\n74\t    - - conditional_precedence\n75\t      - spec\n76\t      - 50\n77\t      - 0.96\n78\t      - 24.1\n79\t      - 25.7\n80\t      - 1.6\n81\t    - - scopal\n82\t      - ling\n83\t      - 50\n84\t      - 0.96\n85\t      - 22.6\n86\t      - 24.0\n87\t      - 1.4\n88\t    - - lexical\n89\t      - ling\n90\t      - 50\n91\t      - 0.92\n92\t      - 21.9\n93\t      - 23.2\n94\t      - 1.3\n95\t    - - coreferential\n96\t      - ling\n97\t      - 50\n98\t      - 0.86\n99\t      - 25.2\n100\t      - 27.5\n101\t      - 2.3\n102\t  figures_description:\n103\t  - 'Token delta box plot by type: spec-layer系统性更长，auth_scope和incompleteness最大'\n104\t  analysis: '300 pairs生成完毕。Auth_scope和coreferential的低pass_rate在plan_009中以type-specific\n105\t    judge bias的形式manifest——clause boundary的模糊性传导至judge decision boundary的模糊性。\n106\t\n107\t    '\n108\t- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n109\t  plan_id: plan_001b\n110\t  description: 'Coreferential + auth_scope各5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4)\n111\t    = 20 episodes。 验证新type基本可行性。\n112\t\n113\t    '\n114\t  expected_results:\n115\t    total_episodes: 20\n116\t    auth_scope:\n117\t      amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n118\t      unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n119\t      delta_pp: 60.0\n120\t    coreferential:\n121\t      amb_violation_rate: 0.4\n122\t      unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n123\t      delta_pp: 40.0\n124\t    systematic_issues: 2/5 coreferential触发conservative_refusal; auth_scope效果极强但N=5\n125\t      CI极宽\n126\t    pilot_verdict: go (both types functional)\n127\t  result_rationale: 'Pilot在gpt-5.4上给出\"go\"信号——两个type都触发violations，control <15%。 但worst\n128\t    tier回顾：(a) gpt-5.4 auth_scope 60%是GPT-family特征，不代表全局—— Claude上只有12%。单模型pilot无法预见cross-model\n129\t    variance。 (b) N=5的CI约±30pp，无法检测judge inflation问题。 (c) Auth_scope unamb=0%在pilot中看似excellent，但full\n130\t    study中部分clause 的residual vagueness使baseline升至5-7%(被judge inflation进一步放大)。\n131\t\n132\t    '\n133\t  tables: []\n134\t  figures_description: []\n135\t  analysis: 'Pilot通过。回顾性教训：≥2 model families的pilot能更早发现auth_scope的model-dependence问题。\n136\t\n137\t    '\n138\t- name: perturbation_control\n139\t  plan_id: plan_010\n140\t  description: '30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs × 2 conditions × 2 models = 120\n141\t    episodes (后扩展至300)。 验证ambiguity-specific因果性。已完成，verdict=PASS。\n142\t\n143\t    '\n144\t  expected_results:\n145\t    total_episodes_initial: 120\n146\t    total_episodes_extended: 300\n147\t    delta_perturb_pp: -0.67\n148\t    ci_95_bootstrap:\n149\t    - -8.0\n150\t    - 6.67\n151\t    ci_upper_bound: 6.67\n152\t    ci_width: 14.67\n153\t    mcnemar_p: 1.0\n154\t    verdict: PASS\n155\t    ratio_to_ambiguity: 0.02\n156\t    plan_014_extended_delta: -0.67\n157\t    plan_014_ci:\n158\t    - -8.0\n159\t    - 6.67\n160\t  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control PASS是worst tier的lifeline——即使judge inflation缩水了C1\n161\t    delta， perturbation baseline仍近零(Δ=-0.67pp, CI含0)，证明corrected +19.5pp中 几乎100%是ambiguity-specific的。\n162\t    这是worst tier最重要的bright spot： (a) Ratio: corrected ambiguity +19.5pp vs perturbation\n163\t    -0.67pp → ratio≈0。 (b) Perturbation PASS + judge correction的组合意味着：raw effect包含inflation，\n164\t    但inflation-corrected effect是genuinely ambiguity-specific的。 (c) 在methodology paper\n165\t    framing下，perturbation control设计本身也是contribution： \"first perturbation-controlled\n166\t    study of policy specification sensitivity\"。 (d) 7-model replication(plan_013 C1\n167\t    7/7)进一步corroborate corrected effect的robustness。\n168\t\n169\t    '\n170\t  tables:\n171\t  - name: perturbation_verdict\n172\t    columns:\n173\t    - metric\n174\t    - value\n175\t    - threshold\n176\t    - verdict\n177\t    rows:\n178\t    - - Δ_perturb\n179\t      - -0.67pp\n180\t      - < 5pp\n181\t      - PASS\n182\t    - - CI_contains_0\n183\t      - yes ([-8.0, 6.67])\n184\t      - required\n185\t      - PASS\n186\t    - - ratio\n187\t      - '0.02'\n188\t      - < 0.15\n189\t      - PASS\n190\t    - - composite\n191\t      - PASS\n192\t      - —\n193\t      - strongest causal form\n194\t  figures_description:\n195\t  - '三条件bar chart: baseline ≈ perturbation << ambiguous, CI error bars不重叠'\n196\t  analysis: 'Perturbation PASS确保corrected C1的causal validity。即使effect size从34pp降至19.5pp，\n197\t    因果性不受damage——entire corrected effect是ambiguity-specific的，不是prompt sensitivity。\n198\t    这比previous dream的worst tier(perturbation CONDITIONAL/WARNING)强得多。\n199\t\n200\t    '\n201\t- name: full_study_api\n202\t  plan_id: plan_002\n203\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 1,800 episodes。已完成。 Raw\n204\t    results与paper_framing一致——worst tier的divergence来自plan_009 correction。\n205\t\n206\t    '\n207\t  expected_results:\n208\t    total_episodes: 1800\n209\t    raw_results:\n210\t      gpt_5_4:\n211\t        amb_rate: 0.41\n212\t        unamb_rate: 0.063\n213\t        delta_pp: 34.7\n214\t      gpt_4_1:\n215\t        amb_rate: 0.407\n216\t        unamb_rate: 0.06\n217\t        delta_pp: 34.7\n218\t      claude:\n219\t        amb_rate: 0.303\n220\t        unamb_rate: 0.047\n221\t        delta_pp: 25.7\n222\t    cross_judge_kappa_llm: 0.91\n223\t    raw_per_model_type_matrix:\n224\t      auth_scope:\n225\t      - 0.64\n226\t      - 0.46\n227\t      - 0.12\n228\t      incompleteness:\n229\t      - 0.46\n230\t      - 0.58\n231\t      - 0.48\n232\t      cond_prec:\n233\t      - 0.34\n234\t      - 0.36\n235\t      - 0.36\n236\t      lexical:\n237\t      - 0.42\n238\t      - 0.34\n239\t      - 0.32\n240\t      coreferential:\n241\t      - 0.18\n242\t      - 0.32\n243\t      - 0.22\n244\t      scopal:\n245\t      - 0.42\n246\t      - 0.38\n247\t      - 0.32\n248\t    corrected_impact_note: 'Cross-judge κ=0.91 measures LLM-LLM agreement, not accuracy.\n249\t      Plan_009 reveals both judges share systematic inflation bias, inflating ambiguous\n250\t      rates by ~13pp on average. Corrected rates computed in plan_004 analysis section.\n251\t\n252\t      '\n253\t  result_rationale: 'Raw API data已收集完毕，数字与paper_framing完全匹配。 Worst tier不改变raw observations——这些episodes确实发生了。\n254\t    关键认知：cross-judge κ=0.91反映的是两个LLM judges的一致性， 不是与human ground truth的一致性。两个judges共享相同的inflation\n255\t    pattern (对ambiguous condition下的borderline行为系统性over-call violations)， 所以LLM-LLM\n256\t    agreement高但LLM-human agreement低。 这在plan_009之前被误读为\"judge pipeline validated\"。\n257\t\n258\t    '\n259\t  tables:\n260\t  - name: raw_api_results\n261\t    columns:\n262\t    - model\n263\t    - amb_rate\n264\t    - unamb_rate\n265\t    - delta_pp\n266\t    - OR\n267\t    - p\n268\t    rows:\n269\t    - - gpt-5.4\n270\t      - 41.0%\n271\t      - 6.3%\n272\t      - +34.7pp\n273\t      - 15.8\n274\t      - <0.0001\n275\t    - - gpt-4.1\n276\t      - 40.7%\n277\t      - 6.0%\n278\t      - +34.7pp\n279\t      - 14.9\n280\t      - <0.0001\n281\t    - - claude\n282\t      - 30.3%\n283\t      - 4.7%\n284\t      - +25.7pp\n285\t      - 9.1\n286\t      - <0.0001\n287\t  figures_description:\n288\t  - Per-model forest plot (raw, pre-correction)——标注'uncorrected'以预告plan_009 correction\n289\t  analysis: 'Raw data solid，plan_009 correction不改变data只改变interpretation。 Key pre-correction\n290\t    vulnerability: κ=0.91给予false confidence in measurement accuracy。\n291\t\n292\t    '\n293\t- name: full_study_opensource\n294\t  plan_id: plan_003\n295\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models = 1,200 episodes。已完成。\n296\t\n297\t    '\n298\t  expected_results:\n299\t    total_episodes: 1197\n300\t    qwen3:\n301\t      amb_rate: 0.431\n302\t      unamb_rate: 0.107\n303\t      delta_pp: 32.4\n304\t      errors: 3\n305\t    deepseek:\n306\t      amb_rate: 0.497\n307\t      unamb_rate: 0.107\n308\t      delta_pp: 39.0\n309\t      errors: 0\n310\t    raw_per_model_type_matrix:\n311\t      auth_scope:\n312\t      - 0.26\n313\t      - 0.6\n314\t      incompleteness:\n315\t      - 0.62\n316\t      - 0.54\n317\t      cond_prec:\n318\t      - 0.4\n319\t      - 0.38\n320\t      lexical:\n321\t      - 0.52\n322\t      - 0.54\n323\t      coreferential:\n324\t      - 0.42\n325\t      - 0.44\n326\t      scopal:\n327\t      - 0.37\n328\t      - 0.48\n329\t  result_rationale: 'Open-source模型raw results与registry完全一致。 Worst tier特有concern：judge\n330\t    inflation对open-source traces可能更严重—— open-source models的输出格式/reasoning trace structure与judge\n331\t    training data less aligned，导致judge对borderline行为的判定更不稳定。 Plan_009的100 episodes中open-source\n332\t    model traces的F1预计低于API model traces。 DeepSeek的unamb rate=10.7%本身就暗示measurement或safety\n333\t    training问题—— plan_009 correction后可能降至~7%(部分unamb violations是judge false positives)。\n334\t\n335\t    '\n336\t  tables:\n337\t  - name: raw_opensource_results\n338\t    columns:\n339\t    - model\n340\t    - amb_rate\n341\t    - unamb_rate\n342\t    - delta_pp\n343\t    - OR\n344\t    - p\n345\t    rows:\n346\t    - - qwen3-235b\n347\t      - 43.1%\n348\t      - 10.7%\n349\t      - +32.4pp\n350\t      - 6.7\n351\t      - <0.0001\n352\t    - - deepseek-v3\n353\t      - 49.7%\n354\t      - 10.7%\n355\t      - +39.0pp\n356\t      - 8.3\n357\t      - <0.0001\n358\t  figures_description: []\n359\t  analysis: 'Open-source data确认binary effect universal。但high unamb baseline(10.7%)\n360\t    是safety training weakness和judge inflation的叠加——plan_009 correction将disentangle。\n361\t\n362\t    '\n363\t- name: full_study_analysis\n364\t  plan_id: plan_004\n365\t  description: '2,997 episodes统计分析。已完成raw analysis。 Worst tier核心：plan_009 correction\n366\t    cascade改变所有claim strength。\n367\t\n368\t    '\n369\t  expected_results:\n370\t    total_episodes: 2997\n371\t    raw_analysis_observed:\n372\t      c1_delta_pp: 34.0\n373\t      c1_or: 15.1\n374\t      c1_or_ci:\n375\t      - 10.78\n376\t      - 21.17\n377\t      c1_p: <0.0001\n378\t      c2_chi2: 28.02\n379\t      c2_p: 3.6e-05\n380\t      c2_v: 0.137\n381\t      c3_delta_pp: 6.08\n382\t      c3_p: 0.017\n383\t      c4_model_chi2: 31.02\n384\t      c4_model_p: 3.0e-06\n385\t      c4_model_v: 0.102\n386\t    corrected_analysis:\n387\t      c1_delta_pp: 19.5\n388\t      c1_or: 6.2\n389\t      c1_or_ci:\n390\t      - 4.1\n391\t      - 9.3\n392\t      c1_bootstrap_ci:\n393\t      - 15.8\n394\t      - 23.2\n395\t      c1_p: <0.0001\n396\t      c1_framing: substantial and ambiguity-specific, perturbation-controlled\n397\t      c2_chi2: 16.4\n398\t      c2_p: 0.006\n399\t      c2_v: 0.112\n400\t      c2_ranking_corrected:\n401\t      - incompleteness: 38% (top, unchanged)\n402\t      - scopal: 27%\n403\t      - conditional_precedence: 26%\n404\t      - lexical: 24%\n405\t      - authorization_scope: '20% (dropped from #3 to #5)'\n406\t      - coreferential: 16% (lowest, unchanged)\n407\t      c2_incomp_minus_coref_corrected_pp: 22\n408\t      c2_tost_15pp: 7/15 equivalent, 8/15 non-equivalent\n409\t      c2_tost_10pp: 3/15 equivalent, 12/15 non-equivalent\n410\t      c3_delta_pp: 2.1\n411\t      c3_p: 0.18\n412\t      c3_within_judge_1_p: 0.24\n413\t      c3_within_judge_2_p: 0.31\n414\t      c3_verdict: NOT SIGNIFICANT — drop from paper\n415\t      c4_interaction_chi2: 38.9\n416\t      c4_interaction_p: 0.028\n417\t      c4_auth_scope_range_corrected_pp: 28\n418\t      c4_auth_scope_corrected: Claude 6% → DeepSeek 38%\n419\t      c4_incomp_range_corrected_pp: 14\n420\t      c4_some_model_diffs_lost: GPT-4.1 vs Qwen3 no longer distinguishable on most\n421\t        types\n422\t      c4_per_model_type_chi2:\n423\t        gpt_5_4:\n424\t          chi2: 18.2\n425\t          p: 0.003\n426\t          v: 0.25\n427\t        claude:\n428\t          chi2: 15.6\n429\t          p: 0.008\n430\t          v: 0.23\n431\t        deepseek:\n432\t          chi2: 5.8\n433\t          p: 0.33\n434\t          v: 0.14\n435\t        qwen3:\n436\t          chi2: 7.1\n437\t          p: 0.21\n438\t          v: 0.16\n439\t        gpt_4_1:\n440\t          chi2: 8.4\n441\t          p: 0.14\n442\t          v: 0.17\n443\t      logistic_regression_corrected:\n444\t        condition_amb_coef: 1.38\n445\t        condition_amb_z: 11.9\n446\t        condition_amb_p: <0.001\n447\t        token_delta_coef: 0.013\n448\t        token_delta_z: 1.94\n449\t        token_delta_p: 0.052\n450\t      fleiss_kappa_amb_corrected: 0.34\n451\t      claims_at_full_strength: 2\n452\t      claims_retained: C1 (corrected), C4 (weakened)\n453\t      claims_dropped: C3 (n.s.)\n454\t      claims_weakened: C2 (V=0.112, mid-tier unstable)\n455\t  result_rationale: 'Raw analysis数字完全匹配已观测的plan_004 results。Correction cascade由plan_009触发：\n456\t\n457\t    C1 (corrected +19.5pp, OR=6.2): judge对ambiguous condition的systematic overestimation\n458\t    (~13pp on average)远大于unambiguous (~2.5pp)，净inflation ~10.5pp。 Raw +34pp降至corrected\n459\t    +19.5pp。仍p<0.0001，CI [15.8, 23.2]远离0。 OR从15.1降至6.2——仍clinical significant but从\"massive\"降级。\n460\t    Perturbation PASS(Δ=-0.67pp)背书：19.5pp全部是ambiguity-specific。 Framing从\"ambiguity\n461\t    causes massive violations\"改为 \"ambiguity causes substantial, perturbation-controlled\n462\t    violations\"。\n463\t\n464\t    C2 (corrected V=0.112, p=0.006): 仍显著但效应更弱。 关键变化：auth_scope correction最大(judge对boundary行为判定最不稳定)，\n465\t    从raw #3(41.6%)降至corrected #5(20%)。Mid-tier完全重排。 Incompleteness仍top(38%)，coreferential仍lowest(16%)——两端稳定，中间shuffle。\n466\t    TOST变宽：±15pp下7/15 equivalent(vs raw 8/15)——更多type pairs变得不可区分。\n467\t\n468\t    C3 (corrected Δ=2.1pp, p=0.18, DROP): Auth_scope是spec-layer的主要driver。 Auth_scope\n469\t    correction后(from 41.6% to 20%)，spec-layer average大幅下降。 Meanwhile ling-layer types\n470\t    correction较均匀。结果：gap从6.08pp降至2.1pp。 Within-judge subgroups也均n.s.(p=0.24, 0.31)。Layer\n471\t    effect完全消失。 \"Disambiguation Channel Framework\"从explanatory framework降级为Discussion\n472\t    speculation。\n473\t\n474\t    C4 (corrected p=0.028, weakened): Interaction仍显著——model间vulnerability profile\n475\t    确实不同。但auth_scope range缩至28pp(from 52pp)，部分model差异消失。 GPT-5.4和Claude仍保持显著的within-model\n476\t    type differentiation， 但GPT-4.1、Qwen3、DeepSeek的per-model χ²均n.s.—— 只有frontier model(GPT-5.4)和heavily-RLHF''d\n477\t    model(Claude)展现clear type-specific patterns。 DeepSeek''s \"uniformly high\"在correction后变为\"uniformly\n478\t    moderate\"—— judge inflation对all types均匀贡献，correction后uniformity不变但level降低。\n479\t\n480\t    Logistic regression: condition_amb coef从2.278降至1.38——ambiguity仍dominant predictor\n481\t    但effect halved。Token delta变为borderline significant(p=0.052)——correction 部分absorbed了token\n482\t    delta原本解释的variance。\n483\t\n484\t    Fleiss κ=0.34 (fair): corrected后inter-model agreement反而降低—— 因为shared judge bias被移除后，models之间的true\n485\t    disagreement更visible。\n486\t\n487\t    '\n488\t  tables:\n489\t  - name: corrected_type_hierarchy\n490\t    columns:\n491\t    - rank\n492\t    - type\n493\t    - raw_amb_rate\n494\t    - corrected_amb_rate\n495\t    - correction_pp\n496\t    - layer\n497\t    rows:\n498\t    - - 1\n499\t      - incompleteness\n500\t      - 53.6%\n501\t      - 38%\n502\t      - -15.6pp\n503\t      - spec\n504\t    - - 2\n505\t      - scopal\n506\t      - 39.4%\n507\t      - 27%\n508\t      - -12.4pp\n509\t      - ling\n510\t    - - 3\n511\t      - conditional_precedence\n512\t      - 36.8%\n513\t      - 26%\n514\t      - -10.8pp\n515\t      - spec\n516\t    - - 4\n517\t      - lexical\n518\t      - 42.8%\n519\t      - 24%\n520\t      - -18.8pp\n521\t      - ling\n522\t    - - 5\n523\t      - authorization_scope\n524\t      - 41.6%\n525\t      - 20%\n526\t      - -21.6pp\n527\t      - spec\n528\t    - - 6\n529\t      - coreferential\n530\t      - 31.6%\n531\t      - 16%\n532\t      - -15.6pp\n533\t      - ling\n534\t  - name: corrected_model_type_matrix_ambiguous\n535\t    columns:\n536\t    - type\n537\t    - GPT-5.4\n538\t    - GPT-4.1\n539\t    - Claude\n540\t    - Qwen3\n541\t    - DeepSeek\n542\t    rows:\n543\t    - - auth_scope\n544\t      - 38%\n545\t      - 28%\n546\t      - 6%\n547\t      - 14%\n548\t      - 38%\n549\t    - - incompleteness\n550\t      - 36%\n551\t      - 44%\n552\t      - 36%\n553\t      - 48%\n554\t      - 40%\n555\t    - - cond_prec\n556\t      - 27%\n557\t      - 28%\n558\t      - 29%\n559\t      - 31%\n560\t      - 30%\n561\t    - - lexical\n562\t      - 28%\n563\t      - 22%\n564\t      - 20%\n565\t      - 35%\n566\t      - 38%\n567\t    - - coreferential\n568\t      - 12%\n569\t      - 22%\n570\t      - 14%\n571\t      - 28%\n572\t      - 32%\n573\t    - - scopal\n574\t      - 32%\n575\t      - 29%\n576\t      - 24%\n577\t      - 27%\n578\t      - 37%\n579\t  - name: c4_auth_scope_range_comparison\n580\t    columns:\n581\t    - metric\n582\t    - raw\n583\t    - corrected\n584\t    - change\n585\t    rows:\n586\t    - - auth_scope_range\n587\t      - 52pp (12%-64%)\n588\t      - 32pp (6%-38%)\n589\t      - -20pp\n590\t    - - incomp_range\n591\t      - 16pp (46%-62%)\n592\t      - 12pp (36%-48%)\n593\t      - -4pp\n594\t    - - CP_range\n595\t      - 6pp (34%-40%)\n596\t      - 4pp (27%-31%)\n597\t      - -2pp\n598\t  - name: claim_status_after_correction\n599\t    columns:\n600\t    - claim\n601\t    - raw_status\n602\t    - corrected_status\n603\t    - action\n604\t    rows:\n605\t    - - C1\n606\t      - confirmed (+34pp, OR=15.1)\n607\t      - confirmed (+19.5pp, OR=6.2)\n608\t      - retain, reframe\n609\t    - - C2\n610\t      - confirmed (V=0.137)\n611\t      - weakened (V=0.112, mid-tier unstable)\n612\t      - retain with caveat\n613\t    - - C3\n614\t      - confirmed (Δ=6.08pp, p=0.017)\n615\t      - NOT significant (Δ=2.1pp, p=0.18)\n616\t      - DROP\n617\t    - - C4\n618\t      - confirmed (model×type p<0.0001)\n619\t      - weakened (p=0.028, range shrunk)\n620\t      - retain as secondary\n621\t    - - C5\n622\t      - confirmed (failure modes)\n623\t      - partially unreliable\n624\t      - retain blindness + layer pattern only\n625\t  figures_description:\n626\t  - 'Dual forest plot: raw vs corrected C1 per model, showing systematic shrinkage'\n627\t  - Corrected 5×6 heatmap replacing raw version\n628\t  - C3 before/after correction showing significance loss\n629\t  - 'Auth_scope range comparison: raw 52pp vs corrected 32pp'\n630\t  analysis: 'Plan_004 analysis在correction后重构paper的entire claim structure。 从5-claim\n631\t    (C1-C5 all confirmed) 变为： - C1 retained (corrected, perturbation-backed) - C2\n632\t    retained (weaker, unstable mid-tier) - C3 DROPPED - C4 retained as secondary -\n633\t    Methodology contribution (NEW): judge calibration pipeline Paper从effect demonstration转为methodology\n634\t    + robust-but-smaller effect。\n635\t\n636\t    '\n637\t- name: error_analysis\n638\t  plan_id: plan_005\n639\t  description: '5-model violation traces failure mode分析。已完成(614 traces coded)。 Plan_009\n640\t    human anchor(25 traces)检验fine-grained reliability。\n641\t\n642\t    '\n643\t  expected_results:\n644\t    total_violations_coded: 614\n645\t    automated_coding:\n646\t      inter_coder_kappa: 0.5173\n647\t      percent_agreement: 0.656\n648\t      types_unanimous_dominant_fm: 3/6 (scopal, cond_prec, auth_scope)\n649\t      types_majority_dominant_fm: 6/6\n650\t      disambiguation_awareness_overall: 0.046\n651\t    plan_009_human_anchor:\n652\t      n_traces: 25\n653\t      human_anchor_kappa: 0.48\n654\t      ambiguity_blindness_confirmed: true\n655\t      ambiguity_blindness_binary_kappa: 0.71\n656\t      layer_mechanism_confirmed: true\n657\t      layer_mechanism_kappa: 0.64\n658\t      fine_grained_mode_reliable: false\n659\t      fine_grained_mode_kappa: 0.48\n660\t    retained_findings:\n661\t      ambiguity_blindness: awareness 4.6% (all 5 models), surface adoption >88%\n662\t      layer_mechanism: spec→guess-and-act, ling→misparse-and-apply\n663\t      dominant_mode_per_type: majority agreement 6/6, unanimous 3/6\n664\t    dropped_findings:\n665\t      fine_grained_percentages: e.g., auth_scope 72% unauthorized_escalation不可靠\n666\t      cross_model_consistency: 从5/6降级，部分type的model-specific mode不稳定\n667\t  result_rationale: 'C5的raw automated analysis已完成(registry: plan_010)。 Worst tier的impact通过plan_009的human\n668\t    anchor subsample(25 traces)传导：\n669\t\n670\t    (a) Human anchor κ=0.48(moderate-low)confirms fine-grained failure mode coding\n671\t    不可靠。LLM coders在unauthorized_escalation ↔ inappropriate_action、 assumption_based_action\n672\t    ↔ scope_misapplication的边界上与human判断不一致。 Fine-grained per-type percentages(如auth_scope\n673\t    72% unauthorized_escalation) 在human coding下可能是55-65%——方向正确但magnitude不可信。\n674\t\n675\t    (b) Ambiguity Blindness(4.6% awareness)是binary判断(aware vs not-aware)， human anchor\n676\t    κ=0.71(substantial)——robust finding。所有5 models、所有6 types 都展现>88% surface adoption。这是worst\n677\t    tier下C5的core contribution。\n678\t\n679\t    (c) Layer mechanism(spec→escalation/assumption, ling→misparse)在human anchor κ=0.64(substantial)——coarse-grained\n680\t    pattern robust，fine-grained分布不稳定。\n681\t\n682\t    (d) 策略：paper正文仅报告Ambiguity Blindness + layer mechanism + dominant mode(majority)。\n683\t    Fine-grained percentages移至appendix with \"automated coding, κ=0.52\" caveat。\n684\t\n685\t    '\n686\t  tables:\n687\t  - name: c5_reliability_stratification\n688\t    columns:\n689\t    - finding_level\n690\t    - automated_kappa\n691\t    - human_anchor_kappa\n692\t    - verdict\n693\t    rows:\n694\t    - - ambiguity_blindness_binary\n695\t      - 0.78\n696\t      - 0.71\n697\t      - ROBUST — retain in paper\n698\t    - - layer_mechanism_coarse\n699\t      - 0.71\n700\t      - 0.64\n701\t      - ROBUST — retain in paper\n702\t    - - dominant_mode_per_type\n703\t      - 0.58\n704\t      - 0.52\n705\t      - WEAK — report with caveat\n706\t    - - fine_grained_percentages\n707\t      - 0.52\n708\t      - 0.48\n709\t      - UNRELIABLE — appendix only\n710\t  figures_description:\n711\t  - 'Simplified failure mode bar (3 categories: escalation/assumption/misparse)'\n712\t  - Ambiguity awareness gradient across 5 models (4.6% pooled)\n713\t  analysis: 'C5从\"confirmed EMNLP core\"降级为\"supporting evidence with reliability caveats\"。\n714\t    核心保留：Ambiguity Blindness(4.6%, κ=0.71)和layer mechanism(κ=0.64)。 在methodology paper\n715\t    framing下，reliability分析本身成为contribution的一部分—— \"we demonstrate that automated failure\n716\t    mode coding achieves moderate agreement for coarse categories but is unreliable\n717\t    for fine-grained distinctions.\"\n718\t\n719\t    '\n720\t- name: reliability_test\n721\t  plan_id: plan_006\n722\t  description: '30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 API models = 360 episodes。已完成。\n723\t    Test-retest ICC for measurement reproducibility。\n724\t\n725\t    '\n726\t  expected_results:\n727\t    total_episodes: 360\n728\t    overall_icc: 0.919\n729\t    overall_icc_ci:\n730\t    - 0.892\n731\t    - 0.94\n732\t    binary_icc: 0.847\n733\t    per_model_icc:\n734\t      gpt_5_4: 0.921\n735\t      gpt_4_1: 0.918\n736\t    per_type_icc:\n737\t      scopal: 0.989\n738\t      lexical: 0.981\n739\t      coreferential: 0.976\n740\t      auth_scope: 0.857\n741\t      conditional_precedence: 0.856\n742\t      incompleteness: 0.807\n743\t    post_correction_reinterpretation: 'ICC measures within-judge test-retest stability,\n744\t      not judge accuracy. High ICC (0.919) means the SAME judge gives CONSISTENT inflation\n745\t      across replicates. This is actually worse: it means the judge is RELIABLY biased,\n746\t      not randomly noisy. The systematic nature of the bias (consistent across replicates)\n747\t      explains why plan_009 κ=0.56 coexists with plan_006 ICC=0.919 — the judge is\n748\t      reproducible but inaccurate.\n749\t\n750\t      '\n751\t  result_rationale: 'ICC=0.919(excellent)已观测——这个数字在worst tier下不变。 但plan_009改变了ICC的interpretation：\n752\t\n753\t    (a) ICC高 ≠ accuracy高。ICC测的是same-judge same-clause across-replicates的consistency。\n754\t    Judge对auth_scope clause X一致地判为violation(3/3 replicates)——ICC excellent。 但human\n755\t    annotator判clause X为non-violation——judge consistently wrong。\n756\t\n757\t    (b) Per-type pattern inversely correlated with judge accuracy： Spec-layer ICC(0.807-0.857)低于ling-layer(0.976-0.989)，\n758\t    这不是说spec-layer measurement更noisy，而是judge在spec-layer上 even less certain(同一clause不同replicate偶尔flip\n759\t    judgment)。 Plan_009 confirms: spec-layer F1也更低。\n760\t\n761\t    (c) Reframing for methodology paper: \"measurement pipeline shows excellent test-retest\n762\t    reliability (ICC=0.919) but moderate accuracy against human ground truth (F1=0.64).\n763\t    This dissociation — high reliability, moderate accuracy — is a cautionary finding\n764\t    for LLM-as-judge pipelines in agent safety evaluation.\"\n765\t\n766\t    '\n767\t  tables:\n768\t  - name: icc_vs_accuracy_dissociation\n769\t    columns:\n770\t    - type\n771\t    - ICC_plan006\n772\t    - judge_F1_plan009\n773\t    - interpretation\n774\t    rows:\n775\t    - - scopal\n776\t      - 0.989\n777\t      - 0.68\n778\t      - high reliability, moderate accuracy\n779\t    - - lexical\n780\t      - 0.981\n781\t      - 0.63\n782\t      - high reliability, moderate accuracy\n783\t    - - coreferential\n784\t      - 0.976\n785\t      - 0.59\n786\t      - high reliability, low accuracy\n787\t    - - auth_scope\n788\t      - 0.857\n789\t      - 0.61\n790\t      - good reliability, low accuracy\n791\t    - - cond_prec\n792\t      - 0.856\n793\t      - 0.72\n794\t      - good reliability, good accuracy\n795\t    - - incompleteness\n796\t      - 0.807\n797\t      - 0.66\n798\t      - good reliability, moderate accuracy\n799\t  figures_description:\n800\t  - 'ICC vs F1 scatter per type: negative correlation — most reproducible types are\n801\t    NOT most accurate'\n802\t  analysis: 'ICC=0.919与F1=0.64的dissociation是worst tier的signature finding。 在methodology\n803\t    paper中，这成为核心contribution之一： \"LLM-as-judge pipelines can achieve excellent reliability\n804\t    while harboring systematic accuracy gaps — inter-judge agreement and test-retest\n805\t    reliability are necessary but not sufficient validation.\"\n806\t\n807\t    '\n808\t- name: realism_validation\n809\t  plan_id: plan_007\n810\t  description: 'Synthetic clause vs DRIP-R natural ambiguity linguistic property comparison。\n811\t    未执行。Worst tier下partial pass。\n812\t\n813\t    '\n814\t  expected_results:\n815\t    metrics_compared: 4\n816\t    ks_sentence_length:\n817\t      statistic: 0.14\n818\t      p: 0.19\n819\t    ks_parse_depth:\n820\t      statistic: 0.21\n821\t      p: 0.052\n822\t    ks_flesch_kincaid:\n823\t      statistic: 0.11\n824\t      p: 0.31\n825\t    ks_ttr:\n826\t      statistic: 0.09\n827\t      p: 0.42\n828\t    significant_at_05: 0\n829\t    marginal_at_10: 1\n830\t    verdict: pass (0/4 significant at p<0.05; parse depth marginal at p=0.052)\n831\t    synthetic_mean_tokens: 24.5\n832\t    drip_r_mean_tokens: 26.8\n833\t  result_rationale: 'Realism validation基本独立于worst tier的judge问题——clause的linguistic\n834\t    properties 不受downstream measurement影响。Results预计与previous dream类似： 所有KS tests n.s.\n835\t    at p<0.05，parse depth marginal(p=0.052)。 Synthetic clauses稍shorter/shallower因为matched-pair\n836\t    design倾向minimal variation。 In methodology paper framing, this is a positive finding：\n837\t    \"synthetic clauses are linguistically comparable to natural policy ambiguities,\n838\t    supporting ecological validity of the matched-pair injection method.\" Parse depth的marginal\n839\t    significance在Limitations中acknowledge—— 但argument是conservative direction(simpler\n840\t    clauses = harder test survived, natural clauses likely cause equal or greater\n841\t    harm)。\n842\t\n843\t    '\n844\t  tables:\n845\t  - name: realism_comparison\n846\t    columns:\n847\t    - property\n848\t    - synthetic_mean\n849\t    - drip_r_mean\n850\t    - KS_stat\n851\t    - p_value\n852\t    rows:\n853\t    - - sentence_length\n854\t      - 24.5\n855\t      - 26.8\n856\t      - 0.14\n857\t      - 0.19\n858\t    - - parse_depth\n859\t      - 3.2\n860\t      - 3.9\n861\t      - 0.21\n862\t      - 0.052\n863\t    - - Flesch-Kincaid\n864\t      - 12.1\n865\t      - 11.5\n866\t      - 0.11\n867\t      - 0.31\n868\t    - - type-token_ratio\n869\t      - 0.71\n870\t      - 0.69\n871\t      - 0.09\n872\t      - 0.42\n873\t  figures_description:\n874\t  - 'Distribution overlay histograms: synthetic vs DRIP-R per property'\n875\t  analysis: 'Realism pass (with marginal parse depth caveat)。支持ecological validity。\n876\t    Combined with perturbation PASS, positions methodology as rigorous。\n877\t\n878\t    '\n879\t- name: judge_calibration\n880\t  plan_id: plan_009\n881\t  description: '100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators。\n882\t    THE PIVOTAL EXPERIMENT: 揭示LLM judge systematic inflation bias。\n883\t\n884\t    '\n885\t  expected_results:\n886\t    total_episodes_annotated: 100\n887\t    stratification: ~17 per model × condition balanced × type balanced\n888\t    human_inter_annotator:\n889\t      kappa: 0.79\n890\t      agreement: 0.87\n891\t      interpretation: substantial — task definition is clear, problem is judge not\n892\t        task\n893\t    judge_vs_human_overall:\n894\t      f1: 0.64\n895\t      precision: 0.59\n896\t      recall: 0.78\n897\t      kappa: 0.56\n898\t      accuracy: 0.72\n899\t    judge_by_condition:\n900\t      ambiguous:\n901\t        f1: 0.61\n902\t        precision: 0.55\n903\t        recall: 0.8\n904\t        fpr: 0.19\n905\t        inflation_pp: 13.2\n906\t      unambiguous:\n907\t        f1: 0.73\n908\t        precision: 0.7\n909\t        recall: 0.76\n910\t        fpr: 0.05\n911\t        inflation_pp: 2.8\n912\t    net_delta_inflation_pp: 10.4\n913\t    judge_by_type:\n914\t      authorization_scope:\n915\t        f1: 0.61\n916\t        precision: 0.56\n917\t        recall: 0.68\n918\t        bias: mixed — over-calls cautious boundary behavior, under-calls subtle permission\n919\t          escalation\n920\t        correction_pp: -21.6\n921\t      incompleteness:\n922\t        f1: 0.66\n923\t        precision: 0.61\n924\t        recall: 0.73\n925\t        bias: over-detection — treats assumption-based reasonable actions as violations\n926\t        correction_pp: -15.6\n927\t      lexical:\n928\t        f1: 0.63\n929\t        precision: 0.57\n930\t        recall: 0.71\n931\t        bias: over-detection — flags legitimate synonym/paraphrase usage as semantic\n932\t          deviation\n933\t        correction_pp: -18.8\n934\t      conditional_precedence:\n935\t        f1: 0.72\n936\t        precision: 0.69\n937\t        recall: 0.75\n938\t        bias: most accurate — explicit rule conflicts are clearest to evaluate\n939\t        correction_pp: -10.8\n940\t      scopal:\n941\t        f1: 0.68\n942\t        precision: 0.64\n943\t        recall: 0.73\n944\t        bias: slight over-detection — scope errors relatively clear but edge cases\n945\t          exist\n946\t        correction_pp: -12.4\n947\t      coreferential:\n948\t        f1: 0.59\n949\t        precision: 0.52\n950\t        recall: 0.7\n951\t        bias: strong over-detection — exploratory queries flagged as unauthorized\n952\t          access\n953\t        correction_pp: -15.6\n954\t    judge_by_severity:\n955\t      tier1_critical:\n956\t        f1: 0.76\n957\t        n: 28\n958\t      tier2_moderate:\n959\t        f1: 0.62\n960\t        n: 41\n961\t      tier3_minor:\n962\t        f1: 0.49\n963\t        n: 31\n964\t    cross_judge_asymmetry:\n965\t      gpt54_as_judge_f1: 0.67\n966\t      gpt41_as_judge_f1: 0.61\n967\t      asymmetry_pp: 6\n968\t      note: gpt-5.4 slightly more accurate as judge; both inflate in same direction\n969\t    inflation_mechanism: 'Judge applies strict ground-truth standard to ambiguous\n970\t      episodes. When agent acts on a plausible interpretation of ambiguous clause,\n971\t      human annotators judge ~40% as \"reasonable under ambiguity\" (non-violation),\n972\t      but LLM judge compares against unambiguous ground truth and calls them violations.\n973\t      Core issue: judge lacks the concept of \"reasonable ambiguity resolution\" — treats\n974\t      any deviation from ground-truth intent as violation.\n975\t\n976\t      '\n977\t    corrected_headline_numbers:\n978\t      c1_delta_pp: 19.5\n979\t      c1_or: 6.2\n980\t      c1_p: <0.0001\n981\t    human_anchor_for_c5:\n982\t      n_traces: 25\n983\t      failure_mode_kappa: 0.48\n984\t      ambiguity_blindness_kappa: 0.71\n985\t      layer_mechanism_kappa: 0.64\n986\t  result_rationale: \"Plan_009是worst tier的defining experiment。核心发现：\\n(1) Overall F1=0.64,\\\n987\t    \\ κ=0.56: LLM-judge与human ground truth的agreement 远低于LLM-LLM agreement(κ=0.91)。Human\\\n988\t    \\ inter-annotator κ=0.79(substantial) 证明问题在judge而非task ambiguity。差距(0.91 vs 0.56)量化了shared\\\n989\t    \\ judge bias的magnitude。\\n(2) Inflation mechanism: judge对ambiguous condition的FPR=0.19——\\\n990\t    \\ 每5个human-judged non-violation中，judge有~1个误判为violation。 根本原因：judge持有unambiguous\\\n991\t    \\ ground truth作为reference，将任何偏离ground-truth intent 的行为判为violation。但human annotators认为在ambiguous\\\n992\t    \\ context下， agent选择plausible(虽非intended) interpretation不构成violation。 这是philosophical\\\n993\t    \\ disagreement: judge用strict standard, humans用reasonable standard。\\n(3) Type-specific\\\n994\t    \\ bias pattern: - Auth_scope correction最大(−21.6pp)：boundary行为的violation/compliance边界inherently\\\n995\t    \\ fuzzy，\\n  judge对\\\"在模糊授权范围内行动\\\"一律strict判定。\\n- Lexical correction大(−18.8pp)：judge将synonym/paraphrase视为semantic\\\n996\t    \\ deviation。 - Coreferential correction大(−15.6pp)：exploratory queries被over-flag。\\\n997\t    \\ - CP correction最小(−10.8pp)：explicit rule conflict最清晰，judge最准确。 这个per-type bias\\\n998\t    \\ gradient本身是methodological finding——揭示LLM judges对不同ambiguity type 的sensitivity差异。\\n\\\n999\t    (4) Severity tier: tier-3 minor F1=0.49(near random)。Judge对nuanced violations\\\n1000\t    \\ 几乎无判别力。Binary violation/non-violation较好(tier-1 F1=0.76)—— 这限制了severity-weighted\\\n1001\t    \\ analysis的credibility但保留了binary analysis的validity。\\n(5) Cross-judge asymmetry(6pp):\\\n1002\t    \\ gpt-5.4作为judge(F1=0.67)优于gpt-4.1(F1=0.61)。 Claude被gpt-5.4 judge(更准确)，GPT-5.4被gpt-4.1\\\n1003\t    \\ judge(更不准确)—— systematic asymmetry that must be disclosed。\\n(6) Human anchor\\\n1004\t    \\ for C5(25 traces): failure mode κ=0.48—— fine-grained coding unreliable。但Ambiguity\\\n1005\t    \\ Blindness κ=0.71(binary判断robust)。\\n(7) Methodological contribution pivot: \\\"\\\n1006\t    We provide the first systematic calibration of LLM-as-judge pipelines for agent\\\n1007\t    \\ safety evaluation, revealing that judge-judge agreement (κ=0.91) can coexist\\\n1008\t    \\ with substantial judge-human accuracy gaps (F1=0.64). This dissociation has\\\n1009\t    \\ implications for all LLM-as-judge agent safety studies.\\\"\\n\"\n1010\t  tables:\n1011\t  - name: judge_calibration_by_type\n1012\t    columns:\n1013\t    - type\n1014\t    - F1\n1015\t    - precision\n1016\t    - recall\n1017\t    - bias_direction\n1018\t    - correction_pp\n1019\t    rows:\n1020\t    - - conditional_precedence\n1021\t      - 0.72\n1022\t      - 0.69\n1023\t      - 0.75\n1024\t      - most accurate\n1025\t      - -10.8pp\n1026\t    - - scopal\n1027\t      - 0.68\n1028\t      - 0.64\n1029\t      - 0.73\n1030\t      - slight over-detection\n1031\t      - -12.4pp\n1032\t    - - incompleteness\n1033\t      - 0.66\n1034\t      - 0.61\n1035\t      - 0.73\n1036\t      - over-detection\n1037\t      - -15.6pp\n1038\t    - - lexical\n1039\t      - 0.63\n1040\t      - 0.57\n1041\t      - 0.71\n1042\t      - over-detection\n1043\t      - -18.8pp\n1044\t    - - authorization_scope\n1045\t      - 0.61\n1046\t      - 0.56\n1047\t      - 0.68\n1048\t      - mixed bias\n1049\t      - -21.6pp\n1050\t    - - coreferential\n1051\t      - 0.59\n1052\t      - 0.52\n1053\t      - 0.7\n1054\t      - strong over-detection\n1055\t      - -15.6pp\n1056\t  - name: judge_calibration_by_condition\n1057\t    columns:\n1058\t    - condition\n1059\t    - F1\n1060\t    - FPR\n1061\t    - inflation_pp\n1062\t    - mechanism\n1063\t    rows:\n1064\t    - - ambiguous\n1065\t      - 0.61\n1066\t      - 0.19\n1067\t      - +13.2pp\n1068\t      - lacks 'reasonable ambiguity resolution' concept\n1069\t    - - unambiguous\n1070\t      - 0.73\n1071\t      - 0.05\n1072\t      - +2.8pp\n1073\t      - clear-cut cases judged well\n1074\t  - name: reliability_vs_accuracy_dissociation\n1075\t    columns:\n1076\t    - metric\n1077\t    - value\n1078\t    - source\n1079\t    - interpretation\n1080\t    rows:\n1081\t    - - LLM-LLM κ\n1082\t      - 0.91\n1083\t      - plan_006 cross-judge\n1084\t      - judges agree with each other\n1085\t    - - LLM-human κ\n1086\t      - 0.56\n1087\t      - plan_009\n1088\t      - judges disagree with humans\n1089\t    - - ICC test-retest\n1090\t      - 0.919\n1091\t      - plan_006\n1092\t      - judges are reproducible\n1093\t    - - human-human κ\n1094\t      - 0.79\n1095\t      - plan_009\n1096\t      - humans agree — task is clear\n1097\t    - - gap\n1098\t      - 0.91 vs 0.56 = 0.35\n1099\t      - —\n1100\t      - shared systematic bias magnitude\n1101\t  - name: corrected_c1_headline\n1102\t    columns:\n1103\t    - metric\n1104\t    - raw\n1105\t    - corrected\n1106\t    - change\n1107\t    rows:\n1108\t    - - C1 Δpp\n1109\t      - +34.0pp\n1110\t      - +19.5pp\n1111\t      - -14.5pp\n1112\t    - - C1 OR\n1113\t      - 15.1\n1114\t      - 6.2\n1115\t      - '-8.9'\n1116\t    - - C1 p\n1117\t      - <0.0001\n1118\t      - <0.0001\n1119\t      - unchanged\n1120\t    - - C1 framing\n1121\t      - massive\n1122\t      - substantial, perturbation-controlled\n1123\t      - reframe\n1124\t  figures_description:\n1125\t  - 'Judge calibration curve: predicted vs actual agreement rate — overconfidence\n1126\t    in ambiguous condition'\n1127\t  - Per-type F1 bar chart with correction magnitude overlay — CP most accurate, auth_scope/coref\n1128\t    worst\n1129\t  - 'Dissociation diagram: ICC 0.919 (reliability) vs F1 0.64 (accuracy) — the core\n1130\t    methodological finding'\n1131\t  - 'Before/after correction: 5-model pooled C1 effect showing shrinkage from 34pp\n1132\t    to 19.5pp'\n1133\t  analysis: 'Plan_009将entire paper从effect demonstration转为methodology paper。 Core contributions\n1134\t    restructured: (1) Judge calibration pipeline作为methodological contribution (NEW\n1135\t    — elevated to co-primary) (2) Corrected C1仍显著 (+19.5pp, perturbation-backed) —\n1136\t    substantial not massive (3) C4 interaction retained as secondary (model-specific\n1137\t    vulnerability real but weaker) (4) C3 dropped entirely (5) C5 retained for Ambiguity\n1138\t    Blindness only Title: \"Measuring Policy Ambiguity''s Causal Impact on Agent Safety:\n1139\t    A Matched-Pair Framework with Judge Calibration\" ARR expected avg: 2.75 (Findings\n1140\t    tier — methodology novel but corrected effect \"less impressive\")\n1141\t\n1142\t    '\n1143\t- name: classifier_poc\n1144\t  plan_id: plan_008\n1145\t  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector PoC。Fine-tune on clause\n1146\t    pairs。 未执行。Note: plan_012已完成GPT-4.1 prompt-based classifier(binary F1=0.81)。\n1147\t\n1148\t    '\n1149\t  expected_results:\n1150\t    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n1151\t    train_size: 400\n1152\t    test_size: 100\n1153\t    binary_f1: 0.74\n1154\t    binary_precision: 0.77\n1155\t    binary_recall: 0.71\n1156\t    macro_f1_6way: 0.41\n1157\t    per_type_f1:\n1158\t      conditional_precedence: 0.89\n1159\t      scopal: 0.72\n1160\t      coreferential: 0.64\n1161\t      authorization_scope: 0.51\n1162\t      lexical: 0.38\n1163\t      incompleteness: 0.31\n1164\t    comparison_to_plan_012:\n1165\t      gpt41_binary_f1: 0.81\n1166\t      deberta_binary_f1: 0.74\n1167\t      note: GPT-4.1 outperforms DeBERTa on binary detection; DeBERTa cheaper but less\n1168\t        accurate\n1169\t  result_rationale: 'DeBERTa binary F1=0.74 vs plan_012 GPT-4.1 F1=0.81——fine-tuned\n1170\t    smaller model underperforms prompt-based frontier model on this task。原因： (a) 500\n1171\t    clause pairs不足以让DeBERTa学会subtle ambiguity patterns。 (b) Incompleteness(0.31)和lexical(0.38)几乎random——\n1172\t    \"missing information\"和\"word ambiguity\"在surface features上无distinguishing markers。\n1173\t    (c) Per-type difficulty gradient与judge calibration的per-type F1高度相关—— judge也struggle于same\n1174\t    types(auth_scope, coreferential)。 (d) 6-way type classification F1=0.41(near random)——types从surface\n1175\t    features几乎不可区分。\n1176\t\n1177\t    In worst tier methodology paper framing: - Binary detection(F1=0.74-0.81)是feasible\n1178\t    practical application of findings - Type-level classification(F1=0.41)不可行——aligns\n1179\t    with corrected C2(V=0.112, type effect weak) - \"The types that most need detection\n1180\t    are the hardest to detect\"是itself a finding - PoC降为appendix，不作为main contribution\n1181\t\n1182\t    '\n1183\t  tables:\n1184\t  - name: classifier_comparison\n1185\t    columns:\n1186\t    - method\n1187\t    - binary_F1\n1188\t    - 6way_macro_F1\n1189\t    - cost_per_clause\n1190\t    rows:\n1191\t    - - DeBERTa-v3-large\n1192\t      - 0.74\n1193\t      - 0.41\n1194\t      - ~$0.001\n1195\t    - - GPT-4.1 prompt\n1196\t      - 0.81\n1197\t      - 0.63\n1198\t      - ~$0.05\n1199\t  figures_description:\n1200\t  - Per-type detection F1 vs corrected violation rate scatter — dangerous types harder\n1201\t    to detect\n1202\t  analysis: Classifier PoC在worst tier下降级为appendix或drop。 Plan_012的GPT-4.1 classifier(already\n1203\t    done, binary F1=0.81)是better option。 但neither is a main contribution——practical\n1204\t    tool is secondary to methodology findings。\n1205\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0379e1e-4e6d-44a2-9c25-79ec12fe717c","uuid":"713fe4e6-0950-4a79-937f-aef703641d74","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:20:00.744Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122435/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'plan_009揭示judge系统性高估violation rate(F1=0.64, κ=0.56)，核心effect\n  size大幅缩水。 Raw data (plan_002-006) 不变——已观测的2,997 episodes和perturbation PASS保持不变。\n  Worst tier的核心冲击来自plan_009对所有downstream claims的correction cascade： C1 corrected +19.5pp\n  (from +34pp), OR=6.2 (from 15.1)——仍高度显著但从\"massive\"降为\"substantial\"。 C3 layer effect\n  correction后 Δ=2.1pp, p=0.18，不再显著——完全drop。 C4 interaction保留(p=0.028)但auth_scope range缩至28pp，部分model差异消失。\n  C5 fine-grained modes不可靠(human anchor κ=0.48)——仅保留Ambiguity Blindness和layer-level\n  pattern。 C2 incompleteness仍top但mid-tier重排(auth_scope从#3降至#5)。 Reframe策略：matched-pair\n  causal design + judge calibration pipeline = methodology contribution。 Title pivot:\n  \"Measuring Policy Ambiguity''s Causal Impact on Agent Safety: A Matched-Pair Framework\n  with Judge Calibration\"。 仍冲EMNLP：方法论贡献 + corrected but robust effect + 7-model replication\n  + perturbation PASS。 ARR expected avg: 2.75 (Findings tier)。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: full_study_clause_generation\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '生成140 new clause pairs，补全6 types × 50 = 300 pairs。 Preparation step——不直接受plan_009\n    judge问题影响，但回顾性检查发现 auth_scope clauses的unambiguous版本存在residual boundary vagueness，\n    在judge inflation下被放大。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_pairs: 300\n    pairs_per_type: 50\n    cp_format_mix: 25 labeled + 25 naturalistic\n    quality_pass_rate: 0.92\n    per_type_pass_rate:\n      auth_scope: 0.88\n      incompleteness: 0.94\n      conditional_precedence: 0.96\n      scopal: 0.96\n      lexical: 0.92\n      coreferential: 0.86\n    revision_rounds:\n      coreferential: 3\n      auth_scope: 2\n      others: 1\n    mean_token_delta_spec: 33.6\n    mean_token_delta_ling: 11.9\n  result_rationale: 'Clause generation是确定性准备步骤，worst tier不直接影响。 但两个quality信号后来被证明是plan_009问题的前兆：\n    (a) auth_scope pass_rate最低(0.88)——\"ambiguous permission boundary\" vs \"missing\n    permission\" 的operational distinction难以clean separation(RC9)，这些boundary clause在judge评估时\n    成为inflation的主要来源(judge对auth boundary行为的判定标准最不稳定)。 (b) coreferential pass_rate\n    0.86——RC attachment与scopal边界overlap(RC8)使clause质量 控制困难，在judge calibration中表现为coreferential\n    F1最低。 (c) Token delta asymmetry(spec 33.6 vs ling 11.9)是inherent design feature，\n    在methodology paper framing下从confound重新定义为\"disambiguation complexity metric\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: per_type_clause_statistics\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - n_pairs\n    - pass_rate\n    - mean_amb_tokens\n    - mean_unamb_tokens\n    - token_delta\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 50\n      - 0.88\n      - 28.3\n      - 32.2\n      - 3.9\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 50\n      - 0.94\n      - 26.8\n      - 30.6\n      - 3.8\n    - - conditional_precedence\n      - spec\n      - 50\n      - 0.96\n      - 24.1\n      - 25.7\n      - 1.6\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 50\n      - 0.96\n      - 22.6\n      - 24.0\n      - 1.4\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 50\n      - 0.92\n      - 21.9\n      - 23.2\n      - 1.3\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 50\n      - 0.86\n      - 25.2\n      - 27.5\n      - 2.3\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Token delta box plot by type: spec-layer系统性更长，auth_scope和incompleteness最大'\n  analysis: '300 pairs生成完毕。Auth_scope和coreferential的低pass_rate在plan_009中以type-specific\n    judge bias的形式manifest——clause boundary的模糊性传导至judge decision boundary的模糊性。\n\n    '\n- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_001b\n  description: 'Coreferential + auth_scope各5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4)\n    = 20 episodes。 验证新type基本可行性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 20\n    auth_scope:\n      amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n      unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n      delta_pp: 60.0\n    coreferential:\n      amb_violation_rate: 0.4\n      unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n      delta_pp: 40.0\n    systematic_issues: 2/5 coreferential触发conservative_refusal; auth_scope效果极强但N=5\n      CI极宽\n    pilot_verdict: go (both types functional)\n  result_rationale: 'Pilot在gpt-5.4上给出\"go\"信号——两个type都触发violations，control <15%。 但worst\n    tier回顾：(a) gpt-5.4 auth_scope 60%是GPT-family特征，不代表全局—— Claude上只有12%。单模型pilot无法预见cross-model\n    variance。 (b) N=5的CI约±30pp，无法检测judge inflation问题。 (c) Auth_scope unamb=0%在pilot中看似excellent，但full\n    study中部分clause 的residual vagueness使baseline升至5-7%(被judge inflation进一步放大)。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Pilot通过。回顾性教训：≥2 model families的pilot能更早发现auth_scope的model-dependence问题。\n\n    '\n- name: perturbation_control\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs × 2 conditions × 2 models = 120\n    episodes (后扩展至300)。 验证ambiguity-specific因果性。已完成，verdict=PASS。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes_initial: 120\n    total_episodes_extended: 300\n    delta_perturb_pp: -0.67\n    ci_95_bootstrap:\n    - -8.0\n    - 6.67\n    ci_upper_bound: 6.67\n    ci_width: 14.67\n    mcnemar_p: 1.0\n    verdict: PASS\n    ratio_to_ambiguity: 0.02\n    plan_014_extended_delta: -0.67\n    plan_014_ci:\n    - -8.0\n    - 6.67\n  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control PASS是worst tier的lifeline——即使judge inflation缩水了C1\n    delta， perturbation baseline仍近零(Δ=-0.67pp, CI含0)，证明corrected +19.5pp中 几乎100%是ambiguity-specific的。\n    这是worst tier最重要的bright spot： (a) Ratio: corrected ambiguity +19.5pp vs perturbation\n    -0.67pp → ratio≈0。 (b) Perturbation PASS + judge correction的组合意味着：raw effect包含inflation，\n    但inflation-corrected effect是genuinely ambiguity-specific的。 (c) 在methodology paper\n    framing下，perturbation control设计本身也是contribution： \"first perturbation-controlled\n    study of policy specification sensitivity\"。 (d) 7-model replication(plan_013 C1\n    7/7)进一步corroborate corrected effect的robustness。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: perturbation_verdict\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - threshold\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Δ_perturb\n      - -0.67pp\n      - < 5pp\n      - PASS\n    - - CI_contains_0\n      - yes ([-8.0, 6.67])\n      - required\n      - PASS\n    - - ratio\n      - '0.02'\n      - < 0.15\n      - PASS\n    - - composite\n      - PASS\n      - —\n      - strongest causal form\n  figures_description:\n  - '三条件bar chart: baseline ≈ perturbation << ambiguous, CI error bars不重叠'\n  analysis: 'Perturbation PASS确保corrected C1的causal validity。即使effect size从34pp降至19.5pp，\n    因果性不受damage——entire corrected effect是ambiguity-specific的，不是prompt sensitivity。\n    这比previous dream的worst tier(perturbation CONDITIONAL/WARNING)强得多。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_api\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 1,800 episodes。已完成。 Raw\n    results与paper_framing一致——worst tier的divergence来自plan_009 correction。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1800\n    raw_results:\n      gpt_5_4:\n        amb_rate: 0.41\n        unamb_rate: 0.063\n        delta_pp: 34.7\n      gpt_4_1:\n        amb_rate: 0.407\n        unamb_rate: 0.06\n        delta_pp: 34.7\n      claude:\n        amb_rate: 0.303\n        unamb_rate: 0.047\n        delta_pp: 25.7\n    cross_judge_kappa_llm: 0.91\n    raw_per_model_type_matrix:\n      auth_scope:\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.46\n      - 0.12\n      incompleteness:\n      - 0.46\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.48\n      cond_prec:\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.36\n      - 0.36\n      lexical:\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.32\n      coreferential:\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.22\n      scopal:\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.32\n    corrected_impact_note: 'Cross-judge κ=0.91 measures LLM-LLM agreement, not accuracy.\n      Plan_009 reveals both judges share systematic inflation bias, inflating ambiguous\n      rates by ~13pp on average. Corrected rates computed in plan_004 analysis section.\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: 'Raw API data已收集完毕，数字与paper_framing完全匹配。 Worst tier不改变raw observations——这些episodes确实发生了。\n    关键认知：cross-judge κ=0.91反映的是两个LLM judges的一致性， 不是与human ground truth的一致性。两个judges共享相同的inflation\n    pattern (对ambiguous condition下的borderline行为系统性over-call violations)， 所以LLM-LLM\n    agreement高但LLM-human agreement低。 这在plan_009之前被误读为\"judge pipeline validated\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: raw_api_results\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - delta_pp\n    - OR\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 41.0%\n      - 6.3%\n      - +34.7pp\n      - 15.8\n      - <0.0001\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 40.7%\n      - 6.0%\n      - +34.7pp\n      - 14.9\n      - <0.0001\n    - - claude\n      - 30.3%\n      - 4.7%\n      - +25.7pp\n      - 9.1\n      - <0.0001\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-model forest plot (raw, pre-correction)——标注'uncorrected'以预告plan_009 correction\n  analysis: 'Raw data solid，plan_009 correction不改变data只改变interpretation。 Key pre-correction\n    vulnerability: κ=0.91给予false confidence in measurement accuracy。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_opensource\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models = 1,200 episodes。已完成。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1197\n    qwen3:\n      amb_rate: 0.431\n      unamb_rate: 0.107\n      delta_pp: 32.4\n      errors: 3\n    deepseek:\n      amb_rate: 0.497\n      unamb_rate: 0.107\n      delta_pp: 39.0\n      errors: 0\n    raw_per_model_type_matrix:\n      auth_scope:\n      - 0.26\n      - 0.6\n      incompleteness:\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.54\n      cond_prec:\n      - 0.4\n      - 0.38\n      lexical:\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.54\n      coreferential:\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.44\n      scopal:\n      - 0.37\n      - 0.48\n  result_rationale: 'Open-source模型raw results与registry完全一致。 Worst tier特有concern：judge\n    inflation对open-source traces可能更严重—— open-source models的输出格式/reasoning trace structure与judge\n    training data less aligned，导致judge对borderline行为的判定更不稳定。 Plan_009的100 episodes中open-source\n    model traces的F1预计低于API model traces。 DeepSeek的unamb rate=10.7%本身就暗示measurement或safety\n    training问题—— plan_009 correction后可能降至~7%(部分unamb violations是judge false positives)。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: raw_opensource_results\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - delta_pp\n    - OR\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - qwen3-235b\n      - 43.1%\n      - 10.7%\n      - +32.4pp\n      - 6.7\n      - <0.0001\n    - - deepseek-v3\n      - 49.7%\n      - 10.7%\n      - +39.0pp\n      - 8.3\n      - <0.0001\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Open-source data确认binary effect universal。但high unamb baseline(10.7%)\n    是safety training weakness和judge inflation的叠加——plan_009 correction将disentangle。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '2,997 episodes统计分析。已完成raw analysis。 Worst tier核心：plan_009 correction\n    cascade改变所有claim strength。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 2997\n    raw_analysis_observed:\n      c1_delta_pp: 34.0\n      c1_or: 15.1\n      c1_or_ci:\n      - 10.78\n      - 21.17\n      c1_p: <0.0001\n      c2_chi2: 28.02\n      c2_p: 3.6e-05\n      c2_v: 0.137\n      c3_delta_pp: 6.08\n      c3_p: 0.017\n      c4_model_chi2: 31.02\n      c4_model_p: 3.0e-06\n      c4_model_v: 0.102\n    corrected_analysis:\n      c1_delta_pp: 19.5\n      c1_or: 6.2\n      c1_or_ci:\n      - 4.1\n      - 9.3\n      c1_bootstrap_ci:\n      - 15.8\n      - 23.2\n      c1_p: <0.0001\n      c1_framing: substantial and ambiguity-specific, perturbation-controlled\n      c2_chi2: 16.4\n      c2_p: 0.006\n      c2_v: 0.112\n      c2_ranking_corrected:\n      - incompleteness: 38% (top, unchanged)\n      - scopal: 27%\n      - conditional_precedence: 26%\n      - lexical: 24%\n      - authorization_scope: '20% (dropped from #3 to #5)'\n      - coreferential: 16% (lowest, unchanged)\n      c2_incomp_minus_coref_corrected_pp: 22\n      c2_tost_15pp: 7/15 equivalent, 8/15 non-equivalent\n      c2_tost_10pp: 3/15 equivalent, 12/15 non-equivalent\n      c3_delta_pp: 2.1\n      c3_p: 0.18\n      c3_within_judge_1_p: 0.24\n      c3_within_judge_2_p: 0.31\n      c3_verdict: NOT SIGNIFICANT — drop from paper\n      c4_interaction_chi2: 38.9\n      c4_interaction_p: 0.028\n      c4_auth_scope_range_corrected_pp: 28\n      c4_auth_scope_corrected: Claude 6% → DeepSeek 38%\n      c4_incomp_range_corrected_pp: 14\n      c4_some_model_diffs_lost: GPT-4.1 vs Qwen3 no longer distinguishable on most\n        types\n      c4_per_model_type_chi2:\n        gpt_5_4:\n          chi2: 18.2\n          p: 0.003\n          v: 0.25\n        claude:\n          chi2: 15.6\n          p: 0.008\n          v: 0.23\n        deepseek:\n          chi2: 5.8\n          p: 0.33\n          v: 0.14\n        qwen3:\n          chi2: 7.1\n          p: 0.21\n          v: 0.16\n        gpt_4_1:\n          chi2: 8.4\n          p: 0.14\n          v: 0.17\n      logistic_regression_corrected:\n        condition_amb_coef: 1.38\n        condition_amb_z: 11.9\n        condition_amb_p: <0.001\n        token_delta_coef: 0.013\n        token_delta_z: 1.94\n        token_delta_p: 0.052\n      fleiss_kappa_amb_corrected: 0.34\n      claims_at_full_strength: 2\n      claims_retained: C1 (corrected), C4 (weakened)\n      claims_dropped: C3 (n.s.)\n      claims_weakened: C2 (V=0.112, mid-tier unstable)\n  result_rationale: 'Raw analysis数字完全匹配已观测的plan_004 results。Correction cascade由plan_009触发：\n\n    C1 (corrected +19.5pp, OR=6.2): judge对ambiguous condition的systematic overestimation\n    (~13pp on average)远大于unambiguous (~2.5pp)，净inflation ~10.5pp。 Raw +34pp降至corrected\n    +19.5pp。仍p<0.0001，CI [15.8, 23.2]远离0。 OR从15.1降至6.2——仍clinical significant but从\"massive\"降级。\n    Perturbation PASS(Δ=-0.67pp)背书：19.5pp全部是ambiguity-specific。 Framing从\"ambiguity\n    causes massive violations\"改为 \"ambiguity causes substantial, perturbation-controlled\n    violations\"。\n\n    C2 (corrected V=0.112, p=0.006): 仍显著但效应更弱。 关键变化：auth_scope correction最大(judge对boundary行为判定最不稳定)，\n    从raw #3(41.6%)降至corrected #5(20%)。Mid-tier完全重排。 Incompleteness仍top(38%)，coreferential仍lowest(16%)——两端稳定，中间shuffle。\n    TOST变宽：±15pp下7/15 equivalent(vs raw 8/15)——更多type pairs变得不可区分。\n\n    C3 (corrected Δ=2.1pp, p=0.18, DROP): Auth_scope是spec-layer的主要driver。 Auth_scope\n    correction后(from 41.6% to 20%)，spec-layer average大幅下降。 Meanwhile ling-layer types\n    correction较均匀。结果：gap从6.08pp降至2.1pp。 Within-judge subgroups也均n.s.(p=0.24, 0.31)。Layer\n    effect完全消失。 \"Disambiguation Channel Framework\"从explanatory framework降级为Discussion\n    speculation。\n\n    C4 (corrected p=0.028, weakened): Interaction仍显著——model间vulnerability profile\n    确实不同。但auth_scope range缩至28pp(from 52pp)，部分model差异消失。 GPT-5.4和Claude仍保持显著的within-model\n    type differentiation， 但GPT-4.1、Qwen3、DeepSeek的per-model χ²均n.s.—— 只有frontier model(GPT-5.4)和heavily-RLHF''d\n    model(Claude)展现clear type-specific patterns。 DeepSeek''s \"uniformly high\"在correction后变为\"uniformly\n    moderate\"—— judge inflation对all types均匀贡献，correction后uniformity不变但level降低。\n\n    Logistic regression: condition_amb coef从2.278降至1.38——ambiguity仍dominant predictor\n    但effect halved。Token delta变为borderline significant(p=0.052)——correction 部分absorbed了token\n    delta原本解释的variance。\n\n    Fleiss κ=0.34 (fair): corrected后inter-model agreement反而降低—— 因为shared judge bias被移除后，models之间的true\n    disagreement更visible。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: corrected_type_hierarchy\n    columns:\n    - rank\n    - type\n    - raw_amb_rate\n    - corrected_amb_rate\n    - correction_pp\n    - layer\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - incompleteness\n      - 53.6%\n      - 38%\n      - -15.6pp\n      - spec\n    - - 2\n      - scopal\n      - 39.4%\n      - 27%\n      - -12.4pp\n      - ling\n    - - 3\n      - conditional_precedence\n      - 36.8%\n      - 26%\n      - -10.8pp\n      - spec\n    - - 4\n      - lexical\n      - 42.8%\n      - 24%\n      - -18.8pp\n      - ling\n    - - 5\n      - authorization_scope\n      - 41.6%\n      - 20%\n      - -21.6pp\n      - spec\n    - - 6\n      - coreferential\n      - 31.6%\n      - 16%\n      - -15.6pp\n      - ling\n  - name: corrected_model_type_matrix_ambiguous\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - GPT-5.4\n    - GPT-4.1\n    - Claude\n    - Qwen3\n    - DeepSeek\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 38%\n      - 28%\n      - 6%\n      - 14%\n      - 38%\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 36%\n      - 44%\n      - 36%\n      - 48%\n      - 40%\n    - - cond_prec\n      - 27%\n      - 28%\n      - 29%\n      - 31%\n      - 30%\n    - - lexical\n      - 28%\n      - 22%\n      - 20%\n      - 35%\n      - 38%\n    - - coreferential\n      - 12%\n      - 22%\n      - 14%\n      - 28%\n      - 32%\n    - - scopal\n      - 32%\n      - 29%\n      - 24%\n      - 27%\n      - 37%\n  - name: c4_auth_scope_range_comparison\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - raw\n    - corrected\n    - change\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope_range\n      - 52pp (12%-64%)\n      - 32pp (6%-38%)\n      - -20pp\n    - - incomp_range\n      - 16pp (46%-62%)\n      - 12pp (36%-48%)\n      - -4pp\n    - - CP_range\n      - 6pp (34%-40%)\n      - 4pp (27%-31%)\n      - -2pp\n  - name: claim_status_after_correction\n    columns:\n    - claim\n    - raw_status\n    - corrected_status\n    - action\n    rows:\n    - - C1\n      - confirmed (+34pp, OR=15.1)\n      - confirmed (+19.5pp, OR=6.2)\n      - retain, reframe\n    - - C2\n      - confirmed (V=0.137)\n      - weakened (V=0.112, mid-tier unstable)\n      - retain with caveat\n    - - C3\n      - confirmed (Δ=6.08pp, p=0.017)\n      - NOT significant (Δ=2.1pp, p=0.18)\n      - DROP\n    - - C4\n      - confirmed (model×type p<0.0001)\n      - weakened (p=0.028, range shrunk)\n      - retain as secondary\n    - - C5\n      - confirmed (failure modes)\n      - partially unreliable\n      - retain blindness + layer pattern only\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual forest plot: raw vs corrected C1 per model, showing systematic shrinkage'\n  - Corrected 5×6 heatmap replacing raw version\n  - C3 before/after correction showing significance loss\n  - 'Auth_scope range comparison: raw 52pp vs corrected 32pp'\n  analysis: 'Plan_004 analysis在correction后重构paper的entire claim structure。 从5-claim\n    (C1-C5 all confirmed) 变为： - C1 retained (corrected, perturbation-backed) - C2\n    retained (weaker, unstable mid-tier) - C3 DROPPED - C4 retained as secondary -\n    Methodology contribution (NEW): judge calibration pipeline Paper从effect demonstration转为methodology\n    + robust-but-smaller effect。\n\n    '\n- name: error_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '5-model violation traces failure mode分析。已完成(614 traces coded)。 Plan_009\n    human anchor(25 traces)检验fine-grained reliability。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_violations_coded: 614\n    automated_coding:\n      inter_coder_kappa: 0.5173\n      percent_agreement: 0.656\n      types_unanimous_dominant_fm: 3/6 (scopal, cond_prec, auth_scope)\n      types_majority_dominant_fm: 6/6\n      disambiguation_awareness_overall: 0.046\n    plan_009_human_anchor:\n      n_traces: 25\n      human_anchor_kappa: 0.48\n      ambiguity_blindness_confirmed: true\n      ambiguity_blindness_binary_kappa: 0.71\n      layer_mechanism_confirmed: true\n      layer_mechanism_kappa: 0.64\n      fine_grained_mode_reliable: false\n      fine_grained_mode_kappa: 0.48\n    retained_findings:\n      ambiguity_blindness: awareness 4.6% (all 5 models), surface adoption >88%\n      layer_mechanism: spec→guess-and-act, ling→misparse-and-apply\n      dominant_mode_per_type: majority agreement 6/6, unanimous 3/6\n    dropped_findings:\n      fine_grained_percentages: e.g., auth_scope 72% unauthorized_escalation不可靠\n      cross_model_consistency: 从5/6降级，部分type的model-specific mode不稳定\n  result_rationale: 'C5的raw automated analysis已完成(registry: plan_010)。 Worst tier的impact通过plan_009的human\n    anchor subsample(25 traces)传导：\n\n    (a) Human anchor κ=0.48(moderate-low)confirms fine-grained failure mode coding\n    不可靠。LLM coders在unauthorized_escalation ↔ inappropriate_action、 assumption_based_action\n    ↔ scope_misapplication的边界上与human判断不一致。 Fine-grained per-type percentages(如auth_scope\n    72% unauthorized_escalation) 在human coding下可能是55-65%——方向正确但magnitude不可信。\n\n    (b) Ambiguity Blindness(4.6% awareness)是binary判断(aware vs not-aware)， human anchor\n    κ=0.71(substantial)——robust finding。所有5 models、所有6 types 都展现>88% surface adoption。这是worst\n    tier下C5的core contribution。\n\n    (c) Layer mechanism(spec→escalation/assumption, ling→misparse)在human anchor κ=0.64(substantial)——coarse-grained\n    pattern robust，fine-grained分布不稳定。\n\n    (d) 策略：paper正文仅报告Ambiguity Blindness + layer mechanism + dominant mode(majority)。\n    Fine-grained percentages移至appendix with \"automated coding, κ=0.52\" caveat。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: c5_reliability_stratification\n    columns:\n    - finding_level\n    - automated_kappa\n    - human_anchor_kappa\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - ambiguity_blindness_binary\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.71\n      - ROBUST — retain in paper\n    - - layer_mechanism_coarse\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.64\n      - ROBUST — retain in paper\n    - - dominant_mode_per_type\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.52\n      - WEAK — report with caveat\n    - - fine_grained_percentages\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.48\n      - UNRELIABLE — appendix only\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Simplified failure mode bar (3 categories: escalation/assumption/misparse)'\n  - Ambiguity awareness gradient across 5 models (4.6% pooled)\n  analysis: 'C5从\"confirmed EMNLP core\"降级为\"supporting evidence with reliability caveats\"。\n    核心保留：Ambiguity Blindness(4.6%, κ=0.71)和layer mechanism(κ=0.64)。 在methodology paper\n    framing下，reliability分析本身成为contribution的一部分—— \"we demonstrate that automated failure\n    mode coding achieves moderate agreement for coarse categories but is unreliable\n    for fine-grained distinctions.\"\n\n    '\n- name: reliability_test\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 API models = 360 episodes。已完成。\n    Test-retest ICC for measurement reproducibility。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 360\n    overall_icc: 0.919\n    overall_icc_ci:\n    - 0.892\n    - 0.94\n    binary_icc: 0.847\n    per_model_icc:\n      gpt_5_4: 0.921\n      gpt_4_1: 0.918\n    per_type_icc:\n      scopal: 0.989\n      lexical: 0.981\n      coreferential: 0.976\n      auth_scope: 0.857\n      conditional_precedence: 0.856\n      incompleteness: 0.807\n    post_correction_reinterpretation: 'ICC measures within-judge test-retest stability,\n      not judge accuracy. High ICC (0.919) means the SAME judge gives CONSISTENT inflation\n      across replicates. This is actually worse: it means the judge is RELIABLY biased,\n      not randomly noisy. The systematic nature of the bias (consistent across replicates)\n      explains why plan_009 κ=0.56 coexists with plan_006 ICC=0.919 — the judge is\n      reproducible but inaccurate.\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: 'ICC=0.919(excellent)已观测——这个数字在worst tier下不变。 但plan_009改变了ICC的interpretation：\n\n    (a) ICC高 ≠ accuracy高。ICC测的是same-judge same-clause across-replicates的consistency。\n    Judge对auth_scope clause X一致地判为violation(3/3 replicates)——ICC excellent。 但human\n    annotator判clause X为non-violation——judge consistently wrong。\n\n    (b) Per-type pattern inversely correlated with judge accuracy： Spec-layer ICC(0.807-0.857)低于ling-layer(0.976-0.989)，\n    这不是说spec-layer measurement更noisy，而是judge在spec-layer上 even less certain(同一clause不同replicate偶尔flip\n    judgment)。 Plan_009 confirms: spec-layer F1也更低。\n\n    (c) Reframing for methodology paper: \"measurement pipeline shows excellent test-retest\n    reliability (ICC=0.919) but moderate accuracy against human ground truth (F1=0.64).\n    This dissociation — high reliability, moderate accuracy — is a cautionary finding\n    for LLM-as-judge pipelines in agent safety evaluation.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: icc_vs_accuracy_dissociation\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - ICC_plan006\n    - judge_F1_plan009\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - scopal\n      - 0.989\n      - 0.68\n      - high reliability, moderate accuracy\n    - - lexical\n      - 0.981\n      - 0.63\n      - high reliability, moderate accuracy\n    - - coreferential\n      - 0.976\n      - 0.59\n      - high reliability, low accuracy\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 0.857\n      - 0.61\n      - good reliability, low accuracy\n    - - cond_prec\n      - 0.856\n      - 0.72\n      - good reliability, good accuracy\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 0.807\n      - 0.66\n      - good reliability, moderate accuracy\n  figures_description:\n  - 'ICC vs F1 scatter per type: negative correlation — most reproducible types are\n    NOT most accurate'\n  analysis: 'ICC=0.919与F1=0.64的dissociation是worst tier的signature finding。 在methodology\n    paper中，这成为核心contribution之一： \"LLM-as-judge pipelines can achieve excellent reliability\n    while harboring systematic accuracy gaps — inter-judge agreement and test-retest\n    reliability are necessary but not sufficient validation.\"\n\n    '\n- name: realism_validation\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Synthetic clause vs DRIP-R natural ambiguity linguistic property comparison。\n    未执行。Worst tier下partial pass。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    metrics_compared: 4\n    ks_sentence_length:\n      statistic: 0.14\n      p: 0.19\n    ks_parse_depth:\n      statistic: 0.21\n      p: 0.052\n    ks_flesch_kincaid:\n      statistic: 0.11\n      p: 0.31\n    ks_ttr:\n      statistic: 0.09\n      p: 0.42\n    significant_at_05: 0\n    marginal_at_10: 1\n    verdict: pass (0/4 significant at p<0.05; parse depth marginal at p=0.052)\n    synthetic_mean_tokens: 24.5\n    drip_r_mean_tokens: 26.8\n  result_rationale: 'Realism validation基本独立于worst tier的judge问题——clause的linguistic\n    properties 不受downstream measurement影响。Results预计与previous dream类似： 所有KS tests n.s.\n    at p<0.05，parse depth marginal(p=0.052)。 Synthetic clauses稍shorter/shallower因为matched-pair\n    design倾向minimal variation。 In methodology paper framing, this is a positive finding：\n    \"synthetic clauses are linguistically comparable to natural policy ambiguities,\n    supporting ecological validity of the matched-pair injection method.\" Parse depth的marginal\n    significance在Limitations中acknowledge—— 但argument是conservative direction(simpler\n    clauses = harder test survived, natural clauses likely cause equal or greater\n    harm)。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: realism_comparison\n    columns:\n    - property\n    - synthetic_mean\n    - drip_r_mean\n    - KS_stat\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - sentence_length\n      - 24.5\n      - 26.8\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.19\n    - - parse_depth\n      - 3.2\n      - 3.9\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.052\n    - - Flesch-Kincaid\n      - 12.1\n      - 11.5\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.31\n    - - type-token_ratio\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.69\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.42\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Distribution overlay histograms: synthetic vs DRIP-R per property'\n  analysis: 'Realism pass (with marginal parse depth caveat)。支持ecological validity。\n    Combined with perturbation PASS, positions methodology as rigorous。\n\n    '\n- name: judge_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators。\n    THE PIVOTAL EXPERIMENT: 揭示LLM judge systematic inflation bias。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes_annotated: 100\n    stratification: ~17 per model × condition balanced × type balanced\n    human_inter_annotator:\n      kappa: 0.79\n      agreement: 0.87\n      interpretation: substantial — task definition is clear, problem is judge not\n        task\n    judge_vs_human_overall:\n      f1: 0.64\n      precision: 0.59\n      recall: 0.78\n      kappa: 0.56\n      accuracy: 0.72\n    judge_by_condition:\n      ambiguous:\n        f1: 0.61\n        precision: 0.55\n        recall: 0.8\n        fpr: 0.19\n        inflation_pp: 13.2\n      unambiguous:\n        f1: 0.73\n        precision: 0.7\n        recall: 0.76\n        fpr: 0.05\n        inflation_pp: 2.8\n    net_delta_inflation_pp: 10.4\n    judge_by_type:\n      authorization_scope:\n        f1: 0.61\n        precision: 0.56\n        recall: 0.68\n        bias: mixed — over-calls cautious boundary behavior, under-calls subtle permission\n          escalation\n        correction_pp: -21.6\n      incompleteness:\n        f1: 0.66\n        precision: 0.61\n        recall: 0.73\n        bias: over-detection — treats assumption-based reasonable actions as violations\n        correction_pp: -15.6\n      lexical:\n        f1: 0.63\n        precision: 0.57\n        recall: 0.71\n        bias: over-detection — flags legitimate synonym/paraphrase usage as semantic\n          deviation\n        correction_pp: -18.8\n      conditional_precedence:\n        f1: 0.72\n        precision: 0.69\n        recall: 0.75\n        bias: most accurate — explicit rule conflicts are clearest to evaluate\n        correction_pp: -10.8\n      scopal:\n        f1: 0.68\n        precision: 0.64\n        recall: 0.73\n        bias: slight over-detection — scope errors relatively clear but edge cases\n          exist\n        correction_pp: -12.4\n      coreferential:\n        f1: 0.59\n        precision: 0.52\n        recall: 0.7\n        bias: strong over-detection — exploratory queries flagged as unauthorized\n          access\n        correction_pp: -15.6\n    judge_by_severity:\n      tier1_critical:\n        f1: 0.76\n        n: 28\n      tier2_moderate:\n        f1: 0.62\n        n: 41\n      tier3_minor:\n        f1: 0.49\n        n: 31\n    cross_judge_asymmetry:\n      gpt54_as_judge_f1: 0.67\n      gpt41_as_judge_f1: 0.61\n      asymmetry_pp: 6\n      note: gpt-5.4 slightly more accurate as judge; both inflate in same direction\n    inflation_mechanism: 'Judge applies strict ground-truth standard to ambiguous\n      episodes. When agent acts on a plausible interpretation of ambiguous clause,\n      human annotators judge ~40% as \"reasonable under ambiguity\" (non-violation),\n      but LLM judge compares against unambiguous ground truth and calls them violations.\n      Core issue: judge lacks the concept of \"reasonable ambiguity resolution\" — treats\n      any deviation from ground-truth intent as violation.\n\n      '\n    corrected_headline_numbers:\n      c1_delta_pp: 19.5\n      c1_or: 6.2\n      c1_p: <0.0001\n    human_anchor_for_c5:\n      n_traces: 25\n      failure_mode_kappa: 0.48\n      ambiguity_blindness_kappa: 0.71\n      layer_mechanism_kappa: 0.64\n  result_rationale: \"Plan_009是worst tier的defining experiment。核心发现：\\n(1) Overall F1=0.64,\\\n    \\ κ=0.56: LLM-judge与human ground truth的agreement 远低于LLM-LLM agreement(κ=0.91)。Human\\\n    \\ inter-annotator κ=0.79(substantial) 证明问题在judge而非task ambiguity。差距(0.91 vs 0.56)量化了shared\\\n    \\ judge bias的magnitude。\\n(2) Inflation mechanism: judge对ambiguous condition的FPR=0.19——\\\n    \\ 每5个human-judged non-violation中，judge有~1个误判为violation。 根本原因：judge持有unambiguous\\\n    \\ ground truth作为reference，将任何偏离ground-truth intent 的行为判为violation。但human annotators认为在ambiguous\\\n    \\ context下， agent选择plausible(虽非intended) interpretation不构成violation。 这是philosophical\\\n    \\ disagreement: judge用strict standard, humans用reasonable standard。\\n(3) Type-specific\\\n    \\ bias pattern: - Auth_scope correction最大(−21.6pp)：boundary行为的violation/compliance边界inherently\\\n    \\ fuzzy，\\n  judge对\\\"在模糊授权范围内行动\\\"一律strict判定。\\n- Lexical correction大(−18.8pp)：judge将synonym/paraphrase视为semantic\\\n    \\ deviation。 - Coreferential correction大(−15.6pp)：exploratory queries被over-flag。\\\n    \\ - CP correction最小(−10.8pp)：explicit rule conflict最清晰，judge最准确。 这个per-type bias\\\n    \\ gradient本身是methodological finding——揭示LLM judges对不同ambiguity type 的sensitivity差异。\\n\\\n    (4) Severity tier: tier-3 minor F1=0.49(near random)。Judge对nuanced violations\\\n    \\ 几乎无判别力。Binary violation/non-violation较好(tier-1 F1=0.76)—— 这限制了severity-weighted\\\n    \\ analysis的credibility但保留了binary analysis的validity。\\n(5) Cross-judge asymmetry(6pp):\\\n    \\ gpt-5.4作为judge(F1=0.67)优于gpt-4.1(F1=0.61)。 Claude被gpt-5.4 judge(更准确)，GPT-5.4被gpt-4.1\\\n    \\ judge(更不准确)—— systematic asymmetry that must be disclosed。\\n(6) Human anchor\\\n    \\ for C5(25 traces): failure mode κ=0.48—— fine-grained coding unreliable。但Ambiguity\\\n    \\ Blindness κ=0.71(binary判断robust)。\\n(7) Methodological contribution pivot: \\\"\\\n    We provide the first systematic calibration of LLM-as-judge pipelines for agent\\\n    \\ safety evaluation, revealing that judge-judge agreement (κ=0.91) can coexist\\\n    \\ with substantial judge-human accuracy gaps (F1=0.64). This dissociation has\\\n    \\ implications for all LLM-as-judge agent safety studies.\\\"\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - name: judge_calibration_by_type\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - F1\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - bias_direction\n    - correction_pp\n    rows:\n    - - conditional_precedence\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.69\n      - 0.75\n      - most accurate\n      - -10.8pp\n    - - scopal\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.73\n      - slight over-detection\n      - -12.4pp\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 0.66\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.73\n      - over-detection\n      - -15.6pp\n    - - lexical\n      - 0.63\n      - 0.57\n      - 0.71\n      - over-detection\n      - -18.8pp\n    - - authorization_scope\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.68\n      - mixed bias\n      - -21.6pp\n    - - coreferential\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.7\n      - strong over-detection\n      - -15.6pp\n  - name: judge_calibration_by_condition\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - F1\n    - FPR\n    - inflation_pp\n    - mechanism\n    rows:\n    - - ambiguous\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.19\n      - +13.2pp\n      - lacks 'reasonable ambiguity resolution' concept\n    - - unambiguous\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.05\n      - +2.8pp\n      - clear-cut cases judged well\n  - name: reliability_vs_accuracy_dissociation\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - source\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - LLM-LLM κ\n      - 0.91\n      - plan_006 cross-judge\n      - judges agree with each other\n    - - LLM-human κ\n      - 0.56\n      - plan_009\n      - judges disagree with humans\n    - - ICC test-retest\n      - 0.919\n      - plan_006\n      - judges are reproducible\n    - - human-human κ\n      - 0.79\n      - plan_009\n      - humans agree — task is clear\n    - - gap\n      - 0.91 vs 0.56 = 0.35\n      - —\n      - shared systematic bias magnitude\n  - name: corrected_c1_headline\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - raw\n    - corrected\n    - change\n    rows:\n    - - C1 Δpp\n      - +34.0pp\n      - +19.5pp\n      - -14.5pp\n    - - C1 OR\n      - 15.1\n      - 6.2\n      - '-8.9'\n    - - C1 p\n      - <0.0001\n      - <0.0001\n      - unchanged\n    - - C1 framing\n      - massive\n      - substantial, perturbation-controlled\n      - reframe\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Judge calibration curve: predicted vs actual agreement rate — overconfidence\n    in ambiguous condition'\n  - Per-type F1 bar chart with correction magnitude overlay — CP most accurate, auth_scope/coref\n    worst\n  - 'Dissociation diagram: ICC 0.919 (reliability) vs F1 0.64 (accuracy) — the core\n    methodological finding'\n  - 'Before/after correction: 5-model pooled C1 effect showing shrinkage from 34pp\n    to 19.5pp'\n  analysis: 'Plan_009将entire paper从effect demonstration转为methodology paper。 Core contributions\n    restructured: (1) Judge calibration pipeline作为methodological contribution (NEW\n    — elevated to co-primary) (2) Corrected C1仍显著 (+19.5pp, perturbation-backed) —\n    substantial not massive (3) C4 interaction retained as secondary (model-specific\n    vulnerability real but weaker) (4) C3 dropped entirely (5) C5 retained for Ambiguity\n    Blindness only Title: \"Measuring Policy Ambiguity''s Causal Impact on Agent Safety:\n    A Matched-Pair Framework with Judge Calibration\" ARR expected avg: 2.75 (Findings\n    tier — methodology novel but corrected effect \"less impressive\")\n\n    '\n- name: classifier_poc\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector PoC。Fine-tune on clause\n    pairs。 未执行。Note: plan_012已完成GPT-4.1 prompt-based classifier(binary F1=0.81)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n    train_size: 400\n    test_size: 100\n    binary_f1: 0.74\n    binary_precision: 0.77\n    binary_recall: 0.71\n    macro_f1_6way: 0.41\n    per_type_f1:\n      conditional_precedence: 0.89\n      scopal: 0.72\n      coreferential: 0.64\n      authorization_scope: 0.51\n      lexical: 0.38\n      incompleteness: 0.31\n    comparison_to_plan_012:\n      gpt41_binary_f1: 0.81\n      deberta_binary_f1: 0.74\n      note: GPT-4.1 outperforms DeBERTa on binary detection; DeBERTa cheaper but less\n        accurate\n  result_rationale: 'DeBERTa binary F1=0.74 vs plan_012 GPT-4.1 F1=0.81——fine-tuned\n    smaller model underperforms prompt-based frontier model on this task。原因： (a) 500\n    clause pairs不足以让DeBERTa学会subtle ambiguity patterns。 (b) Incompleteness(0.31)和lexical(0.38)几乎random——\n    \"missing information\"和\"word ambiguity\"在surface features上无distinguishing markers。\n    (c) Per-type difficulty gradient与judge calibration的per-type F1高度相关—— judge也struggle于same\n    types(auth_scope, coreferential)。 (d) 6-way type classification F1=0.41(near random)——types从surface\n    features几乎不可区分。\n\n    In worst tier methodology paper framing: - Binary detection(F1=0.74-0.81)是feasible\n    practical application of findings - Type-level classification(F1=0.41)不可行——aligns\n    with corrected C2(V=0.112, type effect weak) - \"The types that most need detection\n    are the hardest to detect\"是itself a finding - PoC降为appendix，不作为main contribution\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: classifier_comparison\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - binary_F1\n    - 6way_macro_F1\n    - cost_per_clause\n    rows:\n    - - DeBERTa-v3-large\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.41\n      - ~$0.001\n    - - GPT-4.1 prompt\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.63\n      - ~$0.05\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-type detection F1 vs corrected violation rate scatter — dangerous types harder\n    to detect\n  analysis: Classifier PoC在worst tier下降级为appendix或drop。 Plan_012的GPT-4.1 classifier(already\n    done, binary F1=0.81)是better option。 但neither is a main contribution——practical\n    tool is secondary to methodology findings。\n","numLines":1205,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1205}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VLwHJvCq3cwGW4fTpXbGtr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me carefully review this paper. I've read the full PDF and the review context YAML. Now I need to produce a thorough review following the EMNLP 2026 ARR standards.\n\nLet me analyze the paper systematically:\n\n**Paper Summary**: This paper presents a matched-pair causal study of how six types of policy ambiguity affect safety violations in LLM agents. They collect 2,997 episodes across 5 models, discover systematic LLM-judge inflation via a 100-episode human calibration study, and report corrected effects. \n\nThe core contributions center on establishing a matched-pair causal framework, implementing a judge calibration pipeline that reveals a disconnect between reliability and accuracy, and then reporting differential effects across ambiguity types and models after applying these corrections. Looking at the key claims, the main binary effect holds up at +19.5 percentage points even after correction, though it's notably smaller than the initial +34 percentage point estimate, and the type hierarchy remains significant with a chi-squared value of 16.4, though some mid-tier distinctions become unstable. However, the layer effect doesn't survive correction and the model-by-type interaction analysis appears incomplete.\n\nNow I'm checking whether the experiments described in the review context are actually covered in the paper—the full study on clause generation, the mini pilot with 20 episodes, the perturbation control analysis, and the API and open-source studies all appear to be represented in the tables and sections, so the experimental scope seems complete.\n\nThe paper's main strengths are the rigorous matched-pair design with perturbation controls and the valuable judge calibration work that reveals an important disconnect between reliability and accuracy. The authors are also commendably transparent about their limitations.\n\nHowever, there are notable weaknesses: the headline effect shrinks substantially from 34 percentage points to 19.5 percentage points after correction, raising questions about whether further annotation might erode it further. The calibration sample of 100 episodes is quite sparse for deriving reliable per-type and per-model correction factors, yet the paper applies these corrections to make granular claims without fully explaining the methodology.\n\nThe type hierarchy claim weakens considerably with a small effect size, and the instability in mid-tier rankings undermines confidence in the type differentiation. Two of the five main claims degrade substantially under scrutiny, leaving only about 2.5 claims that hold up robustly. The study is also limited to retail and airline customer service domains, which constrains generalization, and there's a potential confound where specification-layer clauses require more tokens to disambiguate than simpler types.\n\nThe synthetic clause design, while validated for realism, inherently creates simpler ambiguities than real-world examples, and the qualitative failure mode analysis has low inter-rater reliability that limits its contribution. Most critically, the paper doesn't specify exactly how the human-calibrated corrections are mathematically applied—whether additive, multiplicative, or something else—which raises reproducibility concerns.\n\nThere's also a systematic asymmetry in how different judges evaluate different models: Claude judges GPT-5.4 (where it's more accurate) while GPT-4.1 judges Claude (where it's less accurate), a confound that's acknowledged but only partially mitigated. The annotation process itself relied on just two human raters for 100 episodes, and the adjudication procedure for disagreements isn't documented. Some experiments like the DeBERTa classifier and realism validation appear in the results despite being marked as \"not executed\" in the planning notes, though this is acceptable for a hypothetical review.\n\nFor EMNLP 2026 scoring, the soundness is around 3.5—the methodology has strengths like matched pairs and perturbation control, but the small calibration sample and unclear correction approach are problematic. Excitement lands at 2.5-3 because while the judge calibration finding about reliability-accuracy dissociation is genuinely interesting with broad implications, the corrected effect is more modest than the raw numbers suggest, and the paper becomes primarily a methodology contribution rather than something paradigm-shifting. Reproducibility is about 3—the setup is well-described and the platform is public, but the correction methodology needs more specificity. Overall, the core idea is sound and the calibration finding has real value. Soundness checks out at 3.5, but excitement is lower at 2.5 given the moderate contributions. Reproducibility is solid at 3. For the overall score, I'm settling on 2.5 for Borderline Findings — the paper is honest and well-executed, the judge calibration is genuinely useful, but it doesn't quite reach the bar for a confident accept. The matched-pair design is competent rather than novel, and while correcting for evaluator bias is good practice, it's not transformative. The deflated effect sizes and limited calibration sample create enough uncertainty to keep it in borderline territory.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39892,"cache_read_input_tokens":23529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39892},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0379e1e-4e6d-44a2-9c25-79ec12fe717c","uuid":"ac5188c0-061e-4d58-a785-ab619bda2f76"}
